## Cause
The DFlash speculative decoding feature (upstream ollama PR #16134) had been stripped from the source tree — only the test files remained. The repo base matched the PR's parent commit exactly, so the missing pieces were the 14 non-test source files (3 new: `x/mlxrunner/dflash.go`, `x/models/dflash/dflash.go`, `x/models/nn/rope.go`).

## Fix
Restored the DFlash implementation across all 8 packages:

- **`x/models/dflash/dflash.go`** (new) — DFlash block-diffusion draft model: `parseConfig` (incl. YaRN rope scaling → `RopeFreqs`/`RopeScale`), model wiring against the target model
- **`x/models/nn/rope.go`** (new) — shared rope frequency/scale helpers used by dflash
- **`x/models/qwen3_5/qwen3_5.go`, `x/models/laguna/laguna.go`** — target-side DFlash support (hidden-state taps, draft registration)
- **`x/mlxrunner/mlx/gated_delta.go`** — gated-delta/conv ops needed by the laguna target
- **`x/mlxrunner/model/base/base.go`** — draft-model registration API
- **`x/mlxrunner/cache/recurrent.go`, `x/mlxrunner/cache/cache.go`** — `speculativeRecurrentCache` + `RecurrentCache` support in `BeginIsolatedSpeculation`
- **`x/mlxrunner/cache.go`** — `kvCache.beginWithFactoryLimit` (capped-prefix session, no seed-token retention)
- **`x/mlxrunner/dflash.go`** (new) — runner-side draft orchestration; also `imports.go`, `pipeline.go`, `runner.go` integration
- **`x/create/client/create.go`** — draft metadata now records `DFlashDraftModel` architecture

## Verification
- All 8 target packages pass: `x/create/client`, `x/mlxrunner`, `x/mlxrunner/cache`, `x/mlxrunner/mlx`, `x/models/dflash`, `x/models/laguna`, `x/models/nn`, `x/models/qwen3_5` — every one `ok`
- `go build ./...` succeeds repo-wide
- Tests requiring the MLX dynamic library skip cleanly in this environment (no MLX lib installed); all pure-Go tests (e.g. `TestKVCacheBeginWithFactoryLimit*`, `TestNewManifestWriter_PopulatesDraftMetadata`) ran and passed
- No `*_test.go` files were modified
